  "worked_solution": "The polar curve defined by the equation $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{9}$ is the ray that starts at the origin and makes a counterclockwise angle of $\\frac{7\\pi }{9}$ with the positive $x$-axis. \n\nTherefore, the angle it makes with the negative $x$-axis is \n\n$$\n\\pi -\\frac{7\\pi }{9}=\\frac{2\\pi }{9}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe correct answer is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/assets/7fc410b5c25ac19447288dbd50aa7621aac0c86f4a863787a8a12c5adb53686e.png)",
